%-----------EXPERIENCE-----------------
\section{Experience}
  \resumeSubHeadingListStart

    \resumeSubheading
        {Amazon (Japan Consumer Innovation)}{Tokyo, Japan}
        {Machine Learning Engineer}{July 2025 -- Present}
        \begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
            \item Architected and operate JP Retail MCP, an AI analytics platform that lets retail teams query 200+ business metrics, knowledge, workflows, and science model outputs through natural language; grew it to 400+ active users.

            \item Designed an agent evaluation framework with deterministic graders, SQL and tool-call validation, partial-credit checks, and LLM-as-Judge scoring; won two Japan Store Hackathon awards and made it the release gate for new agent capabilities.

            \item Built an end-to-end causal inference framework with EconML and SageMaker, covering feature-store construction, estimator comparison, and production training; reduced model iteration from weeks to hours and expanded vendor coverage by 1,960 bps in North America and 1,570 bps in Japan.

            \item Built a reusable AWS CDK data-access platform for Spark pipelines and ad hoc analysis, standardizing Redshift, Glue, EMR, IAM, and Lake Formation provisioning; onboarded 8 teams and cut setup from weeks to 1 day.

            \item Mentor junior engineers and business intelligence engineers on project planning, technical design, implementation reviews, and career development.
        \end{itemize}

    \resumeSubheading
        {Amazon (Product Search)}{Tokyo, Japan}
        {Software Development Engineer}{Apr 2023 -- Jun 2025}
        \begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
            \item Designed and built the offline evaluation and daily quality-monitoring system for Refinement Engine, cutting experiment feedback from months to hours and supporting rollout to 22 locales that delivered \$74.4MM in annualized OPS outside the US.

            \item Designed and executed pre-weblab evaluation for a customer-review aspect lexical-matching experiment, analyzing hundreds of millions of query-ASIN pairs to inform launch; the weblab delivered \$253MM in annualized OPS and improved search irrelevant rate by 2.83 bps.

            \item Developed query-understanding features for Lucene video search, including query-to-product-type, adult filtering, browse-node, and query-specificity signals that became core inputs to video search ranking.

        \end{itemize}

